  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "What is the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{12}{7x-8}+\\frac{2}{3}\\,?$\n\nThe range is\n$f(x)\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\cup (${{field-3}}$,\\infty ).$",
  "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac{2}{3},$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,\\frac{2}{3})\\cup (\\frac{2}{3},\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929417/assets/c218be8082733d6e1026b8d6f810d43ba4ea3e10928f43260a34a1c4cde7f7f6.png)",
